id: weather-summoning
name: Weather Summoning
uaType: both
prerequisite: Tier of Power 2+
tpCost: 10
type: outOfSequence
actionCost: 0
kiCostPerBaseTier: 5
# "When you use the Power Up Maneuver, you may change the Battle Weather affecting the entire Battlefield to the Storm or
# Tornado Battle Weather of the Natural Weather Tier until the end of your next turn" - offered on a card after each Power
# Up, out of sequence; set on every character in the scene but you ("You are not affected by the effects of any Battle
# Weather that you create through this effect"), what each had given back at the end of your next turn (chat.mjs
# offerWeatherSummoning, postWeatherSummon, weatherTurnEnd).
summonsWeather: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  After a Power Up, out of sequence: Storm or Tornado (Natural) over the whole Battlefield until the end of your next
  turn - not on you.
text: >
  Weather Summoning: You summon dangerous and destructive weather to do your bidding.
  –Ability Type: Technical/Magical
  –Prerequisites: Tier of Power 2+
  –TP Cost: 10
  –KP Cost: 5(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Out-of-Sequence
  –Action Cost: N/A
  –Minions: Non-Minion
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: When you use the Power Up Maneuver, you may change the Battle Weather affecting the entire Battlefield to the
  Storm or Tornado Battle Weather of the Natural Weather Tier until the end of your next turn.

  You are not affected by the effects of any Battle Weather that you create through this effect.
